error[E0277]: `NonNull<u64>` has no atomic bitwise operations
  --> tests/compile_fail/bitwise_mask_on_a_non_null_pointer.rs:11:14
   |
11 |     next.and(!0b1_usize, Relaxed);
   |          --- ^^^^^^^^^^ `and`, `or`, `xor`, `not`, their `fetch_` forms, and `bit_set`, `bit_clear` and `bit_toggle` need `AtomBitwise`
   |          |
   |          required by a bound introduced by this call
   |
   = help: the trait `AtomBitwise` is not implemented for `NonNull<u64>`
   = note: for your own newtype over a value that has it, derive it: `#[derive(AtomBitwise)]`
   = note: for a raw pointer to a sized type, `and`, `or`, `xor` and their `fetch_` forms take a `usize` mask on its address; for another pointer, keep tags beside it in a derived pointer word, whose tag fields have `or`, `and` and `xor`
   = note: to change the value in a compare-exchange loop, call `update`
   = help: the following other types implement trait `AtomBitwise`:
             Saturating<T>
             Wrapping<T>
             bool
             i16
             i32
             i64
             i8
             isize
           and $N others
   = note: required for `atomix_core::Atomic<NonNull<u64>>` to implement `atomix_core::atomic::capability::TakesBitwiseOperand<NonNull<u64>, NonNull<u64>>`
note: required by a bound in `atomix_core::atomic::capability::<impl atomix_core::Atomic<T>>::and`
  --> src/atomic/capability.rs
   |
   | impl<T: Atom> Atomic<T> {
...
   |     pub const fn and<V, O: RmwOrdering<T>>(&self, operand: V, order: O)
   |     where
   |         Self: [const] TakesBitwiseOperand<T, V>,
